# Personal site (Jekyll)

## Stack

- Jekyll 4.x, Minima theme, `jekyll-seo-tag`
- Content: Markdown/HTML pages, `_data/*.yml`, `assets/`
- Local dev: `bundle exec jekyll serve` from repo root (use `Gemfile`)

## Architecture

- **Data-driven content**: lists (projects, creative works) live in `_data/*.yml`; pages loop with Liquid (`site.data.projects`, `site.data.creative.*`).
- **Do not** use `default: []` in Liquid `assign` (breaks on this setup); use `{% assign x = site.data.foo %}` and check `x.size`.
- **Pages**: front matter with `layout: page` (or `default` for `index.html`), explicit `permalink`, title in English unless user asks otherwise.
- **Nav**: new top-level pages must appear in `_config.yml` → `header_pages` (e.g. `projects.md`, not `project.md`).

## Style & assets

- Prefer shared styles in `assets/main.scss`; avoid large inline `<style>` blocks in `.md` / `index.html`.
- Match existing minimal design (CSS variables, cards, centered `.creative-page` max-width).
- Reuse existing class names (`creative-item`, `creative-list`, `project-card`) before inventing new patterns.

## Git & deploy

- Never commit `_site/`, `.jekyll-cache/`, `vendor/bundle/` (see `.gitignore`).
- Do not `git commit` or `git push` unless the user explicitly asks.
- Commit messages: Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`).

## Scope

- Only change files required for the task; no drive-by refactors or unsolicited markdown docs.
- Do not edit generated `_site/` output.
